     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Blocking h4_1:access and h4_0:pivot makes crown:obtain unreachable, since both of its OR parents are cut. One block is not enough. h4_1 can only be cut with a single block by blocking h4_1 itself; otherwise it needs three blocks (h2_0, h3_0 or h1_0, and h3_1 or one of its parents), because h2_0 is fed directly by edge0. If only h4_1 is blocked, h4_0 is still reachable: h3_2 via h1_2, h3_0 via h1_0, and h3_1 via h2_1 (from h1_1, h1_0, edge1) and h2_2.\"}"
